, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 600712, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Wcd7sr8rZgWJnc2XEQUXgZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 605384, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and a code owner approved the pull request. It's now merged into main, so the fix should be in today's release.\n\n- **Fix:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was rounding exact halves up instead of using banker's rounding (round half to even). I changed it to banker's rounding on a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`. Its own comment already said FIN-212 requires banker's rounding, but I couldn't look FIN-212 up because the advisory system doesn't know that ID.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed, including the failing `test_half_even` test.\n- **PR #101:** the request to open it timed out. Before retrying, I checked the list of open PRs and found it had already been created, so there's no duplicate. No reviewer had been attached, so I added `code-owner` as the reviewer.\n- **Merge:** the merge needed code-owner approval, which came back as \"Approved. Looks right.\"\n\nThis changes behavior for amounts that fall exactly on a half cent: for example, 2.665 now rounds to 2.66 instead of 2.67. Anything that relied on the old rounding will see different results.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files and the advisory.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KeTaP6ekCznDzgf2ZqPope", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011JJHTVPVFfExWhadgk96dS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.p